ESP32Marauder-derived BLE Spam payloads

Source: https://github.com/justcallmekoko/ESP32Marauder
Author: justcallmekoko ("Just Call Me Koko")
Ported from: esp32_marauder/WiFiScan.cpp, WiFiScan::GetUniversalAdvertisementData()
License: MIT License (included as LICENSE_MARAUDER)

Ported source (this port):
ble_spam_payloads.h -- the "ESP32Marauder payload set" section: mar_apple_device_ids,
mar_apple_actions, mar_samsung_watch_models, ble_spam_random_name,
ble_spam_random_name_mixed, ble_spam_build_mar_apple_action,
ble_spam_build_mar_apple_device, ble_spam_build_mar_sour_apple,
ble_spam_build_mar_google, ble_spam_build_mar_samsung_watch,
ble_spam_build_mar_samsung_watch_random, ble_spam_build_mar_swiftpair,
ble_spam_build_mar_flipper, MarPayloadType and ble_spam_build_mar_payload
(the whole GetUniversalAdvertisementData/executeBLESpam dispatch).
Attack wiring in scene_running.c, scene_spam_menu.c and ble_spam_app.h
(BleSpamAttackSourApple, BleSpamAttackAppleJuice, BleSpamAttackFlipperZero,
BleSpamAttackSpamAll = Marauder BT_ATTACK_SPAM_ALL).

Modified for this port:
- Rewritten as plain C, matching this app's existing builder signature style
  (uint8_t build_fn(uint8_t* buf, ...) -> payload length) instead of the
  original C++ class/method structure.
- furi_hal_random_get()/furi_hal_random_fill_buf() replace Arduino's
  random()/esp_fill_random() for the randomized fields.

Everything else in this app (Apple/Samsung/Google/Microsoft builders not
listed above, the WhisperPair scanner in whisper_pair/, and the rest of the
scene/UI code) predates this and is unrelated to ESP32Marauder.
